    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0095" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.2173/8.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussells</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that complying
                    with the Department’s instruction No. 80 of December 3 last,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d20-f1"/> I duly applied to the foreign office for the recognition
                    of Mr. Charles C. Broy as American vice and deputy consul general at Boma,
                    Congo. In reply I received notice of the formal recognition of Mr. Broy in the
                    capacity named. I herewith transmit a copy of a note<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d20-f2"/> from the minister for foreign affairs which accompanied
                    the authorization.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
